    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d692">

                <pb facs="0720" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00 Revolutions/66: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McCafferty</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-01-23T21:00:00-05:00">January 23, 1932—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. Department’s 12, January 23, 6 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d692-f1"/> The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rochester</hi> and two destroyers have now been ordered
                    to proceed immediately to Salvador. They should arrive in Salvadorean waters
                    late Sunday night or early Monday morning. The Commander will communicate with
                    you and with the Commander of the two Canadian destroyers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
